id: jf-7sjs
title: Add bounded real-time Jellyfin event streaming
description: "Expose Jellyfin 10.11.11 WebSocket notifications through a safe, bounded, agent-optimized CLI surface outside the REST OpenAPI contract, with deterministic filtering, keepalive handling, structured streaming formats, schemas, docs, and read-only live validation."
type: Plan
status: closed
priority: 0
tags[7]: agents,events,jellyfin-10.11.11,ndjson,read-only,realtime,websocket
created_at: "2026-07-27T21:16:28.541Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-27T22:09:31.040Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-27T21:50:47.433Z"
author: codex-jellyfin-realtime
estimated_minutes: 480
acceptance_criteria: "jf events exposes discoverable help and machine-readable event-type metadata based on the current official Jellyfin WebSocket protocol; jf events watch authenticates without logging credentials, handles ForceKeepAlive, filters message types, and exits deterministically by count, duration, timeout, or signal; streaming output is validated and automation-safe, with NDJSON as the multi-record contract and bounded JSON/TOON alternatives where appropriate; unit, integration, portable, built-CLI, secret, changelog, package, and read-only live tests pass without mutating Jellyfin data"
definition_of_ready: "Latest stable release, exact official server protocol, official TypeScript SDK behavior, live 10.11.11 setup, PM duplicates, and existing command architecture have been inspected."
goal: jf-mqpo
value: Give agents a low-latency source of Jellyfin state changes instead of polling REST endpoints.
impact: "Adds the major API surface omitted by OpenAPI while preserving privacy, bounded execution, and server safety."
outcome: A production-ready jf events command family with protocol-correct subscriptions and deterministic automation contracts.
why_now: "The existing CLI maps every live REST operation, so WebSocket notifications are the clearest current API-parity gap."
parent: jf-gn5j
reviewer: AI review agents and repository checks
risk: high
confidence: high
sprint: jellyfin-10.11.11
resolution: "Implemented the official Jellyfin 10.11.11 authenticated WebSocket event contract as a bounded typed jf events command family, added deterministic schemas/docs/tests, hardened changelog PM context, and validated against the live server without mutation."
expected_result: "Agents can discover supported event types and consume bounded authenticated real-time Jellyfin events in validated TOON, structured aggregate formats, or NDJSON without credential leakage or server mutation."
actual_result: "jf events types exposes 28 official messages; jf events watch supports filters, three periodic read subscriptions, ForceKeepAlive, strict count/duration/connect/message/rate limits, credential-redacted failures, and passed 183/183 compiled live read-only E2E tests."
